            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for (streaming) platform, then the French for thrilling."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la version originale",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la version originale — \"original-language version\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Je préfère voir les films en version originale. I prefer to watch films in the original language."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often la VO; la VOST has subtitles; la VF is the French dub."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la version originale joins version, from Medieval Latin versiō \"a turning\", from vertere \"to turn\", and originale, from Latin orīgō \"beginning\", from orīrī \"to rise\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
